Track 1: Button-Box Blues
- Story & Context: Young Clementine, a runaway living in the train yards near Mobile, found an old button-box accordion on a discarded passenger car, its bellows sighing with a peculiar, metallic rustle when she played it, drawing the curiosity of a phantom conductor who left a single, tarnished brass button on her makeshift bedroll one cold dawn: "This ol' box just keeps singin' its own lonely tune."
